msgid "**One logging contract in the base roles.** `sys-svc-container` and `sys-svc-journalctl` own it: journald is the Docker daemon's default log driver, every container carries an application tag and labels unconditionally, the journal is persistent, and the `docker.service` rate limit is raised so a burst does not drop lines. Applications that log only to files are switched to stdout or stderr, and nested Docker daemons (the Matrix ansible flavour, `svc-runner`) follow the same contract."
