msgid "**Release pushes on main.** A push to *main* whose head commit starts with *Release version* cancels the running *main* pipeline, so the release starts at once. A release-tagged commit deploys every chunk instead of stopping at the first failed one, and still ends red when any chunk fails, which keeps a broken release from being published. A new integration test requires every release tag from v13.0.0 on to sit on that subject, and the test job now checks out the full history with tags."
msgstr ""

