msgid "**Retention and redaction.** Retention is an inventory parameter per log class with a default of 7 days. Secrets are redacted at the source where an application emits them and again in a central pipeline stage; a canary test proves that a synthetic secret never reaches Loki. The 200-line log excerpt that `sys-ctl-hlth-container` sends with its alerts is redacted by the same rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** ``services.loki.retention`` maps each log class the collector assigns (``access``, ``application``, ``system``, ``security``) to a duration (``<n>h``, ``<n>d`` or ``<n>w``, at least ``24h``), 7 days by default. The ``loki_retention`` filter turns the map into one ``retention_stream`` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** `services.loki.retention` maps each log class the collector assigns (`access`, `application`, `system`, `security`) to a duration (`<n>h`, `<n>d` or `<n>w`, at least `24h`), 7 days by default. The `loki_retention` filter turns the map into one `retention_stream` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention:** Finished, failed and cancelled renders are removed after a configurable number of days."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran ``compose down`` and ``up -d`` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. ``sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft`` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran `compose down` and `up -d` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. `sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
