# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Run-once Setup Logic:** Ensures idempotent execution by controlling task flow with internal flags."
msgstr "**Konfigurasjonslogikk:** Sikrer idempotent utførelse ved å kontrollere oppgaveflyt med interne flagg."

msgid "**Runner build:** A deploy that names ``web-app-semaphore`` among its apps (``PRIMARY_APPS`` of the matrix deploy, the ``--id`` list otherwise, every inventory group without one, read as ``lookup('deployment').primary``) builds the runner on the Infinito.Nexus image of that deploy (``SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG``: ``ci-<sha>`` in CI, ``dev-<sha>`` locally, the release version in production, never ``latest``), so the foreign-server deploy and the app-control templates run that checkout. A deploy that pulls Semaphore in only as a provider of another application reads the runner it deployed from the compose file on the stack host and keeps it, building neither the runner nor its base image, as long as the stack host still holds both images and the runner image carries the ``nexus.infinito.semaphore.runner.inputs`` label of this checkout. That label is the sha256 of every build argument but the base image: the digest of the `runner Dockerfile <./files/runner/Dockerfile>`__, the digest of the scripts in ``files/shell/repository/``, the pinned server image, the runner user, its UID and GID, the repository link and the temporary directory. A missing image, a missing label or another digest rebuilds the runner on the image of this deploy, like Semaphore’s own round, and a kept runner whose tag differs from ``SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG`` is reported by a warning task. With ``SOFTWARE_IMAGE_BUILD`` the base image is built from the checkout only when the stack host lacks it. After the compose stack is up, the deploy untags every tag of the runner image on the stack host and, with ``SOFTWARE_IMAGE_BUILD``, every tag of ``SOFTWARE_IMAGE``, except the runner and base image it runs; an image a container still uses keeps its layers. The Playwright environment carries ``SEMAPHORE_RUNNER_IMAGE_TAG``, and every template run of the specs logs it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Runner build:** A deploy that names `web-app-semaphore` among its apps (`PRIMARY_APPS` of the matrix deploy, the `--id` list otherwise, every inventory group without one, read as `lookup('deployment').primary`) builds the runner on the Infinito.Nexus image of that deploy (`SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG`: `ci-<sha>` in CI, `dev-<sha>` locally, the release version in production, never `latest`), so the foreign-server deploy and the app-control templates run that checkout. A deploy that pulls Semaphore in only as a provider of another application reads the runner it deployed from the compose file on the stack host and keeps it, building neither the runner nor its base image, as long as the stack host still holds both images and the runner image carries the `nexus.infinito.semaphore.runner.inputs` label of this checkout. That label is the sha256 of every build argument but the base image: the digest of the [runner Dockerfile](./files/runner/Dockerfile), the digest of the scripts in `files/shell/repository/`, the pinned server image, the runner user, its UID and GID, the repository link and the temporary directory. A missing image, a missing label or another digest rebuilds the runner on the image of this deploy, like Semaphore's own round, and a kept runner whose tag differs from `SOFTWARE_IMAGE_TAG` is reported by a warning task. With `SOFTWARE_IMAGE_BUILD` the base image is built from the checkout only when the stack host lacks it. After the compose stack is up, the deploy untags every tag of the runner image on the stack host and, with `SOFTWARE_IMAGE_BUILD`, every tag of `SOFTWARE_IMAGE`, except the runner and base image it runs; an image a container still uses keeps its layers. The Playwright environment carries `SEMAPHORE_RUNNER_IMAGE_TAG`, and every template run of the specs logs it."
