msgstr ""

msgid "**Second login:** behind the oauth2 gate the render queue still asks for its own login. It accepts the inventory password of the account; a password changed later in Keycloak does not reach it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret hygiene:** Every stored audit payload is passed through ``utils.agents.redact``, so a token, key or password spooled into a note never reaches the chain; the Keycloak and LDAP admin credentials are read from the environment and never logged."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret hygiene:** Every stored audit payload is passed through `utils.agents.redact`, so a token, key or password spooled into a note never reaches the chain; the Keycloak and LDAP admin credentials are read from the environment and never logged."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret path:** The client secret reaches the container base64-encoded on the task's stdin and travels on as an environment variable named by `container exec -e`, so it is never on an argv. Proxmox VE stores it as `client-key` in `/etc/pve/domains.cfg`, where its own `pveum realm add` keeps it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret path:** The client secret reaches the container base64-encoded on the task’s stdin and travels on as an environment variable named by ``container exec -e``, so it is never on an argv. Proxmox VE stores it as ``client-key`` in ``/etc/pve/domains.cfg``, where its own ``pveum realm add`` keeps it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secrets management with OpenBao.** The new *web-app-openbao* role deploys OpenBao at *openbao.<domain>*. It stores application credentials, API keys and machine identities. People sign in through Keycloak, or through LDAP when OpenLDAP is deployed. Their *administrator*, *operator* or *reader* group decides what they can reach, and signing in without one of those groups grants only the default policy. Services and automation use their own AppRole identities, whose credentials change on every deploy, and no root token is kept after the first deploy. A recovery key kept in the token store lets a later deploy get back in if those credentials are lost. A static seal unseals the node on its own after every restart. An internal PKI can be switched on, and Prometheus alerts when the node is sealed or unreachable. The seal key lives only in the encrypted inventory, and a backup of the store cannot be read without it, so back up the inventory together with the volume. See [web-app-openbao](roles/web-app-openbao/README.md)."
msgstr "**Hemmeligheter ledelse med OpenBao..** Den nye *web-app-openbao* rolleutdelinger OpenBao på *Openbao.<domain>*. Den lagrer søknadsopplysninger, API Nøkkeler og maskinidentiteter. Folk logger inn gjennom Keycloak, eller gjennom LDAP når OpenLDAP er utplassert. Deres *administrator*, *Operatør* eller *Leser* gruppe bestemmer hva de kan nå, og logger på uten en av disse gruppene gir bare standardpolitikken. Tjenester og automatisering bruker sine egne AppRole-identiteter, hvis legitimasjon endres på alle utplasseringer, og ingen rottoken holdes etter den første utplasseringen. En gjenopprettingsnøkkel som holdes i pollettbutikken lar en senere implementasjon komme tilbake hvis disse legitimasjonene er tapt. En statisk forsegling avgir noden på egen hånd etter hver omstart. En intern PKI kan slås på, og Prometheus varsler når noden er forseglet eller ugjennomtrengelig. Tetningsnøkkelen bor bare i den krypterte lageret, og en sikkerhetskopi av butikken kan ikke leses uten den, så sikkerhetskopier lageret sammen med volumet. Se [web-app-openbao](roles/web-app-openbao/README.md).."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secrets reuse the credentials mechanism.** MCP tokens, app-passwords, and OAuth client secrets are declared in each role's [`meta/secrets.yml`](../../roles/web-app-baserow/meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:` block and read via `lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')`. No new secret store is introduced."
msgstr "**Hemmeligheter gjenbruk av legitimasjonsmekanismen.** MCP-tokens, app-passord og OAuth-klienthemmeligheter er erklært i hver rolle [`meta/secrets.yml`](../../roles/web-app-baserow/meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:` Blokkere og lese via `lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')`. Ingen ny hemmelig butikk blir introdusert."

msgid "**Secrets stay out of argv:** forwarded variables reach ``container exec`` by name, their values travel in the environment."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secrets stay out of argv:** forwarded variables reach `container exec` by name, their values travel in the environment."
msgstr ""

