# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a Infinito.Nexus platform operator, I want to provide a fully integrated, production-ready Penpot design and prototyping platform within the Infinito.Nexus ecosystem so that teams can create, collaborate on, and share design projects directly inside their sovereign Infinito.Nexus installation."
msgstr "Som Infinito.Nexus plattform operatør, Jeg ønsker å gi en fullt integrert, produksjon-klar Penpot design og prototyping plattform i Infinito.Nexus økosystem slik at team kan skape, samarbeide om og dele designprosjekter direkte inne i deres suverene Infinito.Nexus installasjon."

msgid "As a PostgreSQL superuser, create the empty target database, owned by the role's database user:"
msgstr ""

msgid "As a PostgreSQL superuser, create the empty target database, owned by the role’s database user:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a consumer of the Infinito.Nexus LLM gateway, I want to send a prompt to one alias and have a fast typed decision pick the model that can actually serve it, so that I neither hard-code a model per call site nor pay a large model to answer a question a small one handles."
msgstr "Som forbruker av Infinito.Nexus LLM gateway, Jeg ønsker å sende en beskjed til ett alias og ha en rask skrevet beslutning velge modellen som faktisk kan tjene det, slik at jeg verken hard-code en modell per anrop nettsted eller betale en stor modell for å svare på et spørsmål en liten en håndtak."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose `meta/services.yml` declares `ldap.enabled` (literal `true` or the dynamic `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` form) to ship a Playwright scenario that exercises the LDAP-bind login path end-to-end, so that the LDAP variant of the role's authentication stack is verified independently from its OIDC counterpart."
msgstr "Som bidragsyter som opprettholder per-role Playwright suite, vil jeg ha alle roller som `meta/services.yml` Deklarasjoner `ldap.enabled` (bokstavelig `true` eller dynamisk `\"{{ 'svc-db-openldap' in group_names }}\"` formular) å sende et Playwright-scenario som utøver den LDAP-bindede innloggingsstien slutt til slutt, slik at LDAP-varianten av rollens autentiseringsstabel verifiseres uavhengig av sin OIDC-motstykke."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor maintaining the per-role Playwright suite, I want every role whose login flow is RBAC-gated (OIDC and/or LDAP) to also exercise the canonical non-admin user `biber` end-to-end, so that the RBAC plumbing from [004 - Generic RBAC role auto-provisioning](README.md#archive) is verified per role rather than only on the privileged-admin path."
msgstr "Som en bidragsyter som opprettholder per-role Playwright suite, vil jeg ha alle roller hvis innloggingsflyt er RBAC-portet (OIDC og/eller LDAP) å utøve den kanoniske ikke-admin bruker `biber` end-to-end, slik at RBAC Flow fra [004 - Generisk RBAC rolle auto-provisioning](README.md#archive) er verifisert per rolle i stedet for bare på den priviligerte admin stien."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor to Infinito.Nexus, I want every role that ships application-level extensions to declare them through one unified `meta/addons/` contract (one file per addon), instead of today's per-app spelling (`addons`, `plugins`, `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) scattered across `meta/services.yml`, `vars/main.yml`, and `tasks/`, so that addons are discoverable, lintable, and testable with a single schema, and so that any addon that bridges into another role declares that dependency explicitly through a service flag in `meta/services.yml`."
msgstr "Som bidragsyter til Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha alle roller som sender søknadsnivå utvidelser til å erklære dem gjennom en enhetlig `meta/addons/` kontrakt (en fil per addon), I stedet for dagens per-app staving (`addons`, `plugins`, `extensions`, `modules`, `mu_plugins`) spredt over `meta/services.yml`, `vars/main.yml`, og `tasks/`, slik at addoner er oppdagelige, lintable og testbare med et enkelt skjema, og slik at enhver addon som broer i en annen rolle erklærer at avhengighet eksplisitt gjennom et tjenesteflagg i `meta/services.yml`.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a contributor, I want a requirements template so that new requirements are consistent and machine-readable."
msgstr "Som bidragsyter vil jeg ha en kravmal slik at nye krav er konsekvente og maskinlesbare."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a developer, I want to run the Infinito.Nexus CI on a dedicated server so that the deploy + test cycle is no longer bound by local hardware restrictions."
msgstr "Som utvikler vil jeg drive Infinito.Nexus CI på en dedikert server slik at distribusjon + testsyklusen ikke lenger er bundet av lokale maskinvarebegrensninger."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a maintainer of Infinito.Nexus, I want every user-facing string that core ships extracted into gettext catalogs and machine-translated by LibreTranslate through `make`, so that the API, the documentation and every consumer app serve all ISO 639-1 languages from one source of truth in this repository."
msgstr "Som vedlikeholder av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha alle brukervendte streng som kjerne skip ekstrahert i gettext kataloger og maskinomsatt av LibreTranslate gjennom `make`, slik at API, dokumentasjonen og hver forbruker app betjener alle ISO 639-1 språk fra én kilde til sannhet i dette lager."

msgid "As a maintainer, I want the full-mesh WireGuard test to run only on the role's own CI row, so that no Compose app row spends deploy time on WireGuard while every role keeps its WireGuard support in production."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want ERPNext (Frappe Framework) integrated as a `web-app-erpnext` role with OpenID Connect identity provider integration so that users can access the ERP through the same Single Sign-On (SSO) mechanism used across the Infinito.Nexus ecosystem, reusing the platform's central database and cache services."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha ERPNext (Framework) Integrert som a `web-app-erpnext` rolle med OpenID Connect-identitetsleverandørintegrasjon slik at brukerne kan få tilgang til ERP gjennom den samme Single Sign-On (SSO) mekanisme som brukes over hele Infinito.Nexus økosystem, gjenbruke plattformens sentrale database og cache tjenester."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Checkmk](https://github.com/Checkmk/checkmk) integrated as a `web-app-checkmk` role with Keycloak SSO (via the oauth2-proxy gate) and native LDAP user management so that operators can run the open-source Checkmk monitoring server behind the platform's central Single Sign-On, validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Jellyfin](https://jellyfin.org) integrated as a `web-app-jellyfin` role with Keycloak-backed Single Sign-On so that users can stream the media server behind the platform's central identity, validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha [Jellyfin](https://jellyfin.org) Integrert som a `web-app-jellyfin` rolle med Keycloak-støttet Single Sign-On slik at brukerne kan streame medieserveren bak plattformens sentrale identitet, validert slutt til slutt med Playwright personas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [Semaphore UI](https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore) integrated as a `web-app-semaphore` role with OpenID Connect (Keycloak) SSO and optional LDAP login so that operators can run Ansible / Terraform / OpenTofu / Bash automation from a web UI behind the platform's central Single Sign-On, reusing the central database, and validated end-to-end with Playwright personas."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha [Semaphore UI](https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore) Integrert som a `web-app-semaphore` rolle med OpenID Connect (Keycloak) SSO og valgfri LDAP-innlogging slik at operatører kan kjøre Ansible / Terraform / OpenTofu / Bash-automatisering fra et web-UI bak plattformens sentrale Single Sign-On, gjenbruke sentraldatabasen og validert slutt-til-ende med Playwright-personas."

msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want [World Monitor](https://github.com/koala73/worldmonitor) integrated as a `web-app-worldmonitor` role behind the platform's Keycloak SSO (via the oauth2-proxy gate) so that users reach the real-time global intelligence dashboard with their existing Infinito.Nexus identity, in compose and in swarm, without a second login."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a `svc-ai-robot` role that turns one dedicated machine into an embodied platform for Hermes, giving the agent scoped-to-full host access so it can explore its own hardware and act in the physical world, so that Hermes can \"come to life\" on a robot while this power stays confined to a dedicated, segmented device and never leaks onto shared infrastructure."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha en `svc-ai-robot` rolle som gjør en dedikert maskin til en innebygd plattform for Hermes, noe som gir agenten omfang-til-full verts tilgang slik at den kan utforske sin egen maskinvare og handle i den fysiske verden, slik at Hermes kan \"komme til live\" på en robot mens denne kraften holder seg begrenset til en dedikert, segmentert enhet og aldri lekker på delt infrastruktur."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a `web-app-homeassistant` role that deploys [Home Assistant](https://www.home-assistant.io/) and exposes its native MCP server, so that agent employees (Hermes on a Pi, [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) and other MCP clients can control home devices as scoped MCP tools without any host access, making the \"isolated home assistant\" scenario concrete."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha en `web-app-homeassistant` rolle som distribuerer [Home Assistant](https://www.home-assistant.io/) og avslører sin opprinnelige MCP server, slik at agenten ansatte (Hermes på Pi, [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) og andre MCP-klienter kan styre hjemmeenheter som omfattende MCP-verktøy uten vertsadgang, noe som gjør \"isolert hjemmeassistent\" scenario konkret."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a self-hostable `web-app-atmo` role that deploys an [atmo.rsvp](https://atmo.rsvp) instance (upstream [flo-bit/atmo-events](https://github.com/flo-bit/atmo-events), the successor to OpenMeet) wired to the platform's existing AT Protocol identity, and a bridge that mirrors calendar events between AT Protocol and Mobilizon, so that events created on my instance appear simultaneously on the AT Protocol (Bluesky) network and the ActivityPub (Fediverse) network from a single source of truth."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha en selvvært `web-app-atmo` Rolle som distribuerer en [atmo.rsvp](https://atmo.rsvp) instans (Oppstrøms [flo-bit/atmo-events](https://github.com/flo-bit/atmo-events), Etterfølgeren til OpenMeet) kablet til plattformens eksisterende AT-protokollidentitet, og en bro som speiler kalenderarrangementer mellom AT-protokollen og Mobilizon, slik at hendelser opprettet i mitt tilfelle vises samtidig på AT-protokollen (Bluesky) nettverk og aktivitetspub (Fediverse) Nettverk fra en enkelt kilde til sannhet."

# ha en enkelt OpenAI-kompatibel LLM-gateway som ruter til enhver modell motor
# (lokal Ollama, LM StudioOpenRouter...), For hver AI-forbruker (OpenWebUI,
# Flowiseog agentens ansatte i [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) mål
# 1 `/v1` sluttpunkt og jeg bytter eller legger til modellbakstykker sentralt
# uten å berøre noen forbruker.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want a single OpenAI-compatible LLM gateway that routes to any model backend (local Ollama, LM Studio, OpenRouter, ...), so that every AI consumer (OpenWebUI, Flowise, and the agent employees in [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) targets one `/v1` endpoint and I swap or add model backends centrally without touching any consumer."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha en enkelt OpenAI-kompatibel LLM-gateway som ruter til enhver modell motor (lokal Ollama, LM StudioOpenRouter...), For hver AI-forbruker (OpenWebUI, Flowiseog agentens ansatte i [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md)) mål 1 `/v1` sluttpunkt og jeg bytter eller legger til modellbakstykker sentralt uten å berøre noen forbruker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want every role with a documented Model Context Protocol (MCP) surface to expose or consume MCP through the platform's standard service, identity, proxy, and test contracts so that AI clients can use application data and actions safely without one-off per-role wiring."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha alle roller med en dokumentert modellkontekstprotokoll (MCP) overflate for å utsette eller konsumere MCP gjennom plattformens standardtjeneste, identitet, proxy og testkontrakter slik at AI-klienter kan bruke applikasjonsdata og handlinger trygt uten one-off per-role ledninger."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want every role with an `application_id` to have an explicit, evidence-based MCP disposition and every suitable application to expose a narrowly curated MCP surface to Open WebUI, Flowise, n8n, and other approved clients so that applications can be connected without turning shared administrator credentials, raw infrastructure APIs, or arbitrary network access into agent tools."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha alle roller med en `application_id` å ha en eksplisitt, evidensbasert MCP disposisjon og enhver egnet påføring for å eksponere en smalt herdet MCP overflate til Open WebUI, Flowise, n8n, og andre godkjente klienter slik at applikasjoner kan kobles til uten å slå delte administratorinformasjon, rå infrastruktur-APIer eller vilkårlig nettverkstilgang til agentverktøy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want the `web-app-matrix` role to gain a second deployment flavor that delegates the heavy lifting to the upstream [matrix-docker-ansible-deploy](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD) playbook, so that the full Matrix ecosystem — Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Jitsi-backed video conferencing, ma1sd / Dimension / hookshot / etcetera — is available without the role re-implementing each service from scratch. The existing role-internal compose stack stays selectable as the `compose` flavor for one cycle, marked deprecated."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator av Infinito.Nexus, Jeg vil ha `web-app-matrix` rolle for å få en annen utplasseringssmak som delegerer den tunge løft til oppstrøms [matrise-docker-assible-depploy](https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy) (MDAD) playbook, så det fulle Matrix økosystem - Synapse, Element, hver støttet bro, Jitsi-støttet videokonferanse, ma1sd / Dimensjon / krokshot / etcetera — er tilgjengelig uten rollen som re-implementere hver tjeneste fra bunnen. Den eksisterende rolle-intern komponeringsstabelen forblir valgbar som den `compose` smak for én syklus, merket utdatert."

msgid "As a platform administrator of Infinito.Nexus, I want to deploy self-hostable AI agent platforms (Hermes Agent, OpenClaw) as kernel-isolated, scalable \"employees\" across my nodes, coordinated by a Flowise supervisor over MCP and routed to models through the [052](052-llm-gateway-model-backends.md) gateway, so that I run a fleet of isolated agents with cross-agent pipelines and kernel-level isolation, without bespoke per-agent wiring."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform administrator, I want Infinito.Nexus to support multi-node Docker Swarm deployments with NFS-backed shared volumes, so that services can be rescheduled across nodes without losing persistent data, scaled horizontally, and updated with rolling updates — gaining high availability without introducing Kubernetes complexity."
msgstr "Som plattformadministrator vil jeg ha Infinito.Nexus å støtte multi-node Docker Swarm distribusjoner med NFS-støttet delte volumer, slik at tjenester kan omorganiseres på tvers av noder uten å miste vedvarende data, skalert horisontalt og oppdatert med rullende oppdateringer — får høy tilgjengelighet uten å introdusere Kubernetes kompleksitet."

msgid "As a platform operator who runs Nextcloud with the `user_oidc` plugin, I want the deployment to register the Keycloak provider in `user_oidc` with Nextcloud's own Keycloak client, so that Nextcloud signs its users in to their existing accounts and ends their sessions when Keycloak sends a back-channel logout token."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a platform operator, I want every address an application trusts for login to be either owned by the platform or proven by its user, and WordPress Multisite to grant each user exactly the rights their groups name on every site of the network, so that no user can take over another account by changing their email and no administrator loses rights by signing in."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a platform operator, I want members of the `operator` role group to pause and resume every deployed Infinito.Nexus application from Semaphore, and members of the `administrator` role group to deploy Infinito.Nexus from Semaphore to a foreign server, so that routine control and remote rollouts run through one audited, role-gated web UI instead of a shell on the host."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a platform operator, I want the ERPNext structure that the core role, the Infinito.Nexus store (GUI) and the security check (Security) build on one ERPNext site to stay compatible, so that no line strips, disables or overwrites what another line created, and every tenant gets only the structure that holds for every tenant."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a platform operator, I want the complete logs of every deployed Infinito.Nexus application collected in one store and searchable, graphable and alertable in Grafana behind Keycloak, so that I can troubleshoot and audit any application on any node without a shell on the host."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a platform operator, I want the sign-in page of every application to offer only the login methods its deployment mode allows, each switchable on its own in `meta/services.yml`, so that users see one way to sign in (the SSO button whenever Keycloak runs) and no side door bypasses the central identity."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a platform user with agent access, I want Open WebUI to start my own Hermes or OpenClaw agent the first time I address it, isolated from every other user's agent, so that I work with a personal agent without an administrator provisioning one for me, while administrators decide through RBAC who may use agents at all."
msgstr "Som plattformbrukere med tilgang til agent vil jeg ha Open WebUI Start min egen Hermes eller OpenClaw agent første gang jeg adresserer det, isolert fra alle andre brukerens agent, slik at jeg jobber med en personlig agent uten en administrator som gir en til meg, mens administratorer bestemmer gjennom RBAC som kan bruke agenter i det hele tatt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a self-hoster running Infinito.Nexus behind NAT/CGNAT/dynamic IP (Raspberry Pi, edge node, home server), I want a `svc-net-tor` role that makes the node's primary domain a Tor v3 `.onion` address so that the entire stack (web, SSO, LDAP, CA) is reachable over Tor without public IP, port forwarding, VPS, or DynDNS — while individual apps can still attach extra public domains with their own TLS."
msgstr "Som egenvert som kjører Infinito.Nexus bak NAT/CGNAT/dynamic IP (Raspberry Pi, kant node, hjemme server), Jeg vil ha en `svc-net-tor` rolle som gjør nodens primære domene til Tor v3 `.onion` adresse slik at hele stabelen (web, SSO, LDAP, CA) er tilgjengelig over Tor uten offentlig IP, portvideresending, VPS eller DyndNS — mens individuelle apper kan fortsatt legge ekstra offentlige domener med sine egne TLS."

msgid "As a signed-in user who reaches an application whose role groups I do not hold, I want to request the roles I need right from the 403 page so that an administrator can review and grant them without a separate channel."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a user of an Infinito.Nexus deployment, I want the Infinito.Nexus beaver to show me what the platform is doing while I wait, when something breaks and when I need help, so that waits are visible, errors read friendly and help is one hover away on every app."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a user of an Infinito.Nexus deployment, I want to ask the beaver in the corner of every app a question and get a short answer with a link to the documentation it comes from, so that I find help without leaving the app or waiting for a person."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a user of the Infinito.Nexus dashboard, I want the applications ordered in nested folders, a search that finds any application at once, a frame in the corporate color, and tiles that tell me whether I may open an application and whether it runs, so that I reach the right application fast and know before the click whether it will work for me."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a user who is signed in through one browser on the clearnet and the onion network, or on several devices, I want two explicit choices at logout, \"Log out on this device\" and \"Log out everywhere\", where the first ends every session of this browser the platform can end server to server and the second also ends every session of mine on all other devices, so that no network or device keeps a live session of mine that I did not choose to keep."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As a visitor of an Infinito.Nexus deployment, I want the documentation, the universal logout panel and the dashboard to speak my language from the core gettext catalogs, and I want browser apps such as MIG to be allowed to read the API, so that every surface core renders follows the same translations."
msgstr "Som besøkende på et Infinito.Nexus implementasjon, Jeg vil at dokumentasjonen, det universelle utloggingspanelet og instrumentbordet skal snakke språket mitt fra kjernen gettext-kataloger, og jeg vil ha nettleserapplikasjoner som MIG å få lov til å lese API, slik at hver overflatekjerne gjør følger de samme oversettelser."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As an Infinito.Nexus administrator, I want [OpenBao](https://github.com/openbao/openbao) deployed as a `web-app-openbao` role with Keycloak OIDC login, group-mapped policies, persistent storage, automatic unsealing, backup and monitoring, so that infrastructure secrets, application credentials, certificates and tokens can be stored and retrieved centrally without distributing static secrets across systems."
msgstr "Som Infinito.Nexus administrator, jeg vil [OpenBao](https://github.com/openbao/openbao) utplassert som a `web-app-openbao` rolle med Keycloak OIDC-innlogging, gruppekartlagte retningslinjer, vedvarende lagring, automatisk utsegling, sikkerhetskopiering og overvåking, slik at infrastrukturhemmeligheter, programinformasjon, sertifikater og tokens kan lagres og hentes sentralt uten å distribuere statiske hemmeligheter over systemer."

msgid "As an administrator or user of an application, I want every field that the deployment, the SSO login or a timer writes into that application's own UI to either reach its source, or be visibly locked with that source named, or be set once and then left to me, so that no change I make silently disappears at the next deploy, login or timer run."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator iterating on one application, I want a deploy to build the Semaphore runner image only when Semaphore's own round needs it or its inputs changed, so that a deploy of an unrelated application on a stack with Semaphore does not spend minutes and gigabytes rebuilding the runner."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of Infinito.Nexus, I want every web UI to follow one configurable corporate design (palette, typography, logo, title, light and dark mode) so that all apps read as one platform while the base color stays changeable from a single setting."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of a Tor node, I want to choose whether the node's outbound traffic leaves directly, sends only `.onion` through Tor, or goes entirely through Tor with no clearnet fallback, and to name the destinations that always or never take Tor, so that the node's own address reaches only the services I accept, and a stopped Tor stops traffic instead of exposing it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "As an operator of a self-hosted deployment, I want every role whose application ships a native AI feature to reach the platform's own LiteLLM gateway instead of a third-party provider, so that prompts, documents and telemetry never leave the deployment and one credential rotation covers every application."
msgstr "Som operatør av en selv-vert utplassering, vil jeg ha alle roller hvis applikasjon sender en innfødt AI-funksjon for å nå plattformens egen LiteLLM gateway i stedet for en tredjepartsleverandør, slik at spør, dokumenter og telemetri aldri forlate utplasseringen og en troverdig rotasjon dekker hvert program."

msgid "As an operator of a swarm deployment, I want `services.openldap.network.public` to open LDAPS on port 636 through openresty as it does in compose, so that LDAP clients outside the cluster reach slapd over TLS while no backend port of OpenLDAP is published."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of an Infinito.Nexus deployment, I want one translation endpoint that chooses the best engine itself, remembers which engine won earlier comparisons, and lets a human override any string, so that every application translates content through a single configured URL and the quality improves without me tuning each application separately."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of an Infinito.Nexus node that runs the Tor provider next to a public clearnet domain, I want every web application to be reachable on clearnet and onion at the same time by default, configured from one place per role, so that clearnet users and Tor users reach the same deployment and every page stays inside the network it was requested on."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of applications that keep customer credentials in [`web-app-openbao`](../../roles/web-app-openbao/), I want every request to OpenBao recorded with the accessing identity and a timestamp, so that each read of a stored secret can be traced to the person or machine that made it."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of compose hosts, laptops and hosts behind NAT, I want `svc-net-wireguard` to build a hub-and-spoke mesh around a host I name, without a swarm manager, so that roaming and NATed members reach every other member through the hub and a deploy never waits on a member that is offline."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator of several hosts, I want galaxyserver, hotelserver and every further host to use the one LiteLLM gateway on echoserver over the WireGuard mesh, each host with its own virtual key, so that models, provider keys and spend live in one place and a small host such as a Raspberry Pi runs no gateway of its own."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator retiring Mailu, I want the Stalwart import to carry over every mailbox in Mailu's maildir volume, not only the inventory accounts, so that mailboxes created through SSO or the Mailu admin UI keep their mail, folders and filters after the switch."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator upgrading a long-running host across several major versions of its applications, I want every deploy to detect the version that the existing data was written by and to step through every mandatory intermediate version on its own, or to stop loudly where no forward path exists, so that one deploy brings old data to the pinned version without manual upgrade stops, silent downgrades or stale code and asset volumes."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator who deploys many applications per host, I want the application stack (front proxy, backend, database) to be one shared `stack` service that the service loader runs once, before the application roles, and that processes every application of the play in that one invocation, so that a deploy stops repeating host-wide stack work per application and the stack has a single point of truth instead of 115 include sites."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator who runs many worktrees and agents on one workstation, I want every local cache to stay within a fixed size, the cache, tools and deploy-runner services to run once per machine as their own stack deployed through the infinito inventory, every test and quality gate to run in one shared long-lived test runner, and every local deploy to run as a job of a runner pool, so that the disk no longer fills up, a gate no longer builds and starts a stack of its own, parallel deploys never collide, and only the stacks a target needs are running."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator who runs several compose slots, swarm lab clusters and GUI lanes on one host, I want repeated package and tool downloads to land in one shared host cache folder and every swarm or roundtrip run to release its cluster once the rescue bundle is saved, so that parallel stacks stop filling the root filesystem."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want a throwaway instance on a developer's machine to run the agents against the board, accounts and storage of a remote live instance, so that developers work with real agents without holding an admin token of the live instance and without losing state at a teardown."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want agents to take work from the OpenProject board, talk and ask for approval through Matrix, email and Zammad, start from a catalog of profiles in Open WebUI, n8n and Flowise, and be managed from Open WebUI, so that humans meet the agents where they already work and keep the approval gates."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want an agent to work in its own virtual machine, on a local Incus host or on Proxmox VE in a data center, so that it can run the whole Infinito.Nexus development and test matrix behind its own kernel and has no path to my workstation's Docker daemon, keys or production vault."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want every AI agent of the platform (team agents, agents users start from a catalog of employee profiles, the robot and coding agents) to be defined in one `agents/` tree, run on one pluggable runtime contract, act under its own account, be steered by deterministic Python routines, take its work from one Kanban board and be bounded by one RBAC-based agent firewall, so that agents can maintain, design, tune and implement the platform autonomously while I control who can do what, where."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want every agent to act under its own account with its own credentials, model key and model list, to work in an isolated workspace and to reach the forges only through its own accounts, so that each agent's reach is bounded by its grants and traceable to it."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want every application that logs a user in from a proxy-set identity header to be reachable only through openresty, and openresty to clear or overwrite that header on every location, so that no client can impersonate a user, for example with `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username: administrator`."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want every make target the routine tool nodes need to exist and every defect the running agents reported in existing targets to be fixed, so that the routines of the agents restructuring call deterministic tooling instead of working around it."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the AI roles to run one LibreTranslate engine, consume the translation gateway, enable their optional Open WebUI services and test peer presence through services lookups, and I want the earlier AI requirements to agree with the agents restructuring, so that the platform and its requirements carry no duplicate or contradicting statement before the board migration."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the Nextcloud Talk high-performance backend and recording server to run as separate services built from semver-pinned upstream sources, with every configuration file rendered by `web-app-nextcloud`, so that the updater can raise their versions automatically and no upstream start script can overwrite the role's configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the `agents/` tree, the lint catalog and the deterministic routine layer of the agent platform to be complete and proven by lints and unit tests without a running stack, so that every later phase of the agents restructuring builds on a verified static layer."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the agent firewall compiler to turn the `allow`, `ask` and `deny` rules of `agents/firewall/` into proven decisions and generated settings, so that every surface the control plane deploys later receives limits that unit tests have already checked."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the agents bundle deployed together with every app of the deploy matrix and the agents' end-to-end chains proven locally through act with local models only, so that the first CI deploy of `feature/agents` starts from a stack that is already green on the developer machine."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the agents restructuring proven by the CI on `infinito-nexus/core`, accepted with my own credentials, and the requirements migrated to the OpenProject board as the last step, so that `feature/agents` merges into `main` with every criterion backed by a recorded proof."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the broker and the orchestrator to discover runtimes, run the agent lifecycle, start routines from triggers and crons, keep routine state across restarts and audit every action, and I want `make agents-verify` to play real scenarios against that stack, so that every later phase is proven by deployed scenarios instead of skipped ones."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want the reviewer, planner, coordinator, operator, tester, translator, documenter, release, security, hacker, counsel, support and tuner roles to run their routines on the deployed platform, so that each role does its documented work end to end under the firewall and the approval gates."
msgstr ""

msgid "As an operator, I want to declare application roles that live in their own repositories, such as the landing page and the store GUI, as ordinary inventory groups that Infinito.Nexus pulls into `roles/web-app-cst-*` and verifies like every in-tree role, so that these projects ship their role from their own repository without a fork of core and without a second, weaker set of checks."
msgstr ""

