msgid "SeaweedFS honours a public-read object or bucket ACL on an unsigned read unless a bucket policy explicitly denies it first. A bare ``Principal: \"*\"`` deny would also hit the consumer's own signed and presigned requests; the ``Null`` condition on ``aws:username`` limits it to unsigned ones, because SeaweedFS derives that key from a signed caller's IAM user ARN and evaluates an unsigned request as principal ``*`` without it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "SeaweedFS is the shared S3 object store. A role becomes a consumer by declaring a `seaweedfs` service in `meta/services.yml`, wiring its app config from `lookup('objstore', application_id, ...)` (bucket / access_key / secret_key / url / region), and shipping a gated `files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`. See `web-app-mastodon`, `web-app-pixelfed`, and `web-app-nextcloud` for the reference pattern. SeaweedFS S3 requires **path-style addressing** and the internal `http://` endpoint."
msgstr "SeaweedFS er delt S3 Objektbutikk. En rolle blir en forbruker ved å erklære en `seaweedfs` service i `meta/services.yml`, ledninger sin app konfigurasjon fra `lookup('objstore', application_id, ...)` (bøtte / access_key / secret_key / url / region), og frakte en portet `files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`. Se `web-app-mastodon`, `web-app-pixelfed`, og `web-app-nextcloud` for referansemønsteret. SeaweedFS S3 krever **Adresse i stistil** den interne `http://` endepunkt."

