msgid "Setup also sends streaming requests and tool-call/result round trips through LiteLLM for Chat Completions, Messages and Responses. These six checks run with the configured validation worker limit and add nine inference requests to the ordinary provider and consumer checks. Errors, missing answer text and unfinished streams fail deployment; sanitized results contain no keys or model text. The checks consume provider quota and may incur charges. Live compatibility depends on the installed FreeLLMAPI version and configured provider pool; the role remains pre-alpha until its full deploy loop is proven."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Several applications have a useful read API but no MCP server, and several projects ship an MCP server that authenticates *to* the application without authenticating the client calling it. Putting either behind this adapter gives the surface a bearer of its own, an exact tool allowlist, and enforced ceilings. The deployment renders one contract per instance, so the same image serves every provider without any of them sharing a credential or a trust boundary."
msgstr "Flere applikasjoner har en nyttig lesing API men ingen MCP-server, og flere prosjekter sender en MCP-server som godkjenner *til* Søknaden uten å godkjenne klienten som kaller det. Setter enten bak denne adapteren gir overflaten en bærer av seg selv, en nøyaktig verktøy tillateliste og håndhevet tak. Utdelingen gjør én kontrakt per instans, så det samme bildet tjener hver leverandør uten at noen av dem deler en troverdig eller en tillitsgrense."

