# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rejected text is a comment and never a ``msgstr``: it is what the consumers must not use, while an operator judging the criterion needs to read it. A newline is escaped because a ``.po`` comment ends at one. The ``nocheck`` goes on a line of its own above the quote, never behind it: a mangled link is exactly what a rejection quotes and the URL probe reads comments too, while a long quote is wrapped over several comment lines, which would carry the marker away from the URL it has to cover."
msgstr "Den avviste teksten er en kommentar og aldri en ``msgstr``: Det er det forbrukerne ikke må bruke, mens en operatør som vurderer kriteriet må lese det. En ny linje er rømt fordi en ``.po`` Kommentaren slutter på én. Den ``nocheck`` går på en linje av sin egen over sitatet, aldri bak det: en manglet link er nøyaktig hva en avvisning sitater og URL-proben leser kommentarer også, mens et langt sitat er pakket over flere kommentarlinjer, som ville bære markøren bort fra URL den må dekke."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rejected text travels with the verdict so the catalog can record it: a bare mark says an entry is unanswerable, the text says what the server answered, which is what an operator needs to judge the criterion."
msgstr "Den avviste teksten reiser med dommen slik at katalogen kan registrere den: et bare merke sier at en oppføring er usvarlig, teksten sier hva serveren svarte, som er hva en operatør trenger å dømme kriteriet."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The relay resolves its upstream per connection. In swarm, `stream{}` gets the Docker embedded resolver through the shared `NETWORK_DOCKER_DNS_NGINX_DIRECTIVE` (`valid=30s`, `ipv6` from `NETWORK_IPV6_ENABLED`); stream needs no values of its own, and the hard-coded resolver line of `http{}` stays outside this requirement. The stream server renders `set $proxy_pass_upstream \"openldap:<ports.internal.ldap>\";` plus `proxy_pass $proxy_pass_upstream;`. The `proxy_pass` lookup renders it with `stream=True` from the same `resolve_upstream` the HTTP vhosts use, so openresty starts while openldap is still down and follows a new task address."
msgstr ""

msgid "The relay widens no proxy trust. The relay network is no role network: `compute_external_network_roles` leaves it out, so the pre-created role overlays and `proxy_hops` of every application, the LDAP clients included, stay byte-identical with the switch on and off. Sharing the openldap overlay instead would have put openresty next to every LDAP client, `svc-ai-agent-provisioner` included, and Docker DNS would then route openresty's HTTP requests to those clients over it, so each client would have to trust that subnet as a proxy. Excluding the subnet from `proxy_hops` while still sharing the overlay was rejected for the same routing reason."
msgstr ""

