msgid "The search panel of the default source never lists a result: a query logs `Connecting to 'https://d1bplzhgyq-dsn.algolia.net/1/indexes/*/queries' violates the following Content Security Policy directive: \"connect-src 'self' https://cdn.<domain>\"` and the list stays empty (measured on the compose stack). Cause: the theme queries the Algolia index of the upstream site from the browser and `meta/csp.yml` declares no `connect-src` entry; an allowed request would return links into upstream's own pages. Options: whitelist the Algolia host under `connect-src` and accept upstream's index; or leave the request blocked and remove the search controls from the build."
