# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This is an accepted trade-off, not an oversight. Moodle offers no allowlist, so a single internal host cannot be permitted without unblocking the range it sits in. The cost is that any account holding a URL-fetching capability, such as ``block/rss_client:myaddinstance`` or a ``repository/url`` instance, can make the server issue requests to sibling containers. Grant those capabilities only to roles you trust with that reach, or keep the upstream blocklist and accept that SSO login and the AI surface do not work."
msgstr "Dette er et akseptert fradrag, ikke et tilsyn. Moodle tilbyr ingen tillatt liste, så en enkelt intern vert kan ikke tillates uten å fjerne blokkering av området den sitter i. Kostnaden er at enhver konto som har en URL-fetching-funksjon, som ``block/rss_client:myaddinstance`` eller a ``repository/url`` kan gjøre serverens utstedelse forespørsler til søskenbeholdere. Gi disse mulighetene bare til roller du stoler på med den rekkevidden, eller hold oppstrømsblokklisten og godta at SSO-innlogging og AI-overflaten ikke fungerer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This is an accepted trade-off, not an oversight. Moodle offers no allowlist, so a single internal host cannot be permitted without unblocking the range it sits in. The cost is that any account holding a URL-fetching capability, such as `block/rss_client:myaddinstance` or a `repository/url` instance, can make the server issue requests to sibling containers. Grant those capabilities only to roles you trust with that reach, or keep the upstream blocklist and accept that SSO login and the AI surface do not work."
