msgid "`Ollama <https://ollama.com>`__ is a local model server that runs open LLMs on your hardware and exposes a simple HTTP API. Prompts and data stay on your machines, making it the backbone for privacy-first AI."
msgstr "`Ollama <https://ollama.com>`__ er en lokal modellserver som kjører åpne LLMs på maskinvaren og avslører en enkel HTTP API. Forespørsler og data blir på maskinene dine, noe som gjør det til ryggraden for personvern-første AI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Open PR if … changed` step"
msgstr "`Open PR if … changed` trinn"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`OpenBao <https://openbao.org/>`__ is an identity-based secrets and encryption manager governed by the Linux Foundation. It stores application credentials, API keys, service and database credentials, automation and agent identities, short-lived tokens and encryption keys behind a policy engine, and can act as an internal certificate authority."
msgstr "`OpenBao <https://openbao.org/>`__ er en identitetsbasert hemmelighet og kryptering manager styrt av Linux Foundation. Det lagrer søknadsopplysninger, API nøkler, service- og databaseinformasjon, automatisering og agentidentiteter, kortlevede poletter og krypteringsnøkler bak en policymotor, og kan fungere som en intern sertifikatmyndighet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`OpenClaw <https://openclaw.ai/>`__ is an open-source personal AI agent that runs on hardware you control. It ships a gateway process with a browser Control UI next to its CLI and TUI, keeps persistent memory and a workspace on disk, and performs browser and filesystem tasks inside its own sandbox."
msgstr "`OpenClaw <https://openclaw.ai/>`__ er et åpen kildekode personlig AI-agent som kjører på maskinvare du kontrollerer. Det sender en gateway-prosess med en nettleserkontroll-UI ved siden av sin CLI og TUI, holder vedvarende minne og et arbeidsområde på disken, og utfører nettleser- og filsystemoppgaver inne i sin egen sandkasse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`OpenCloud <https://opencloud.eu/>`__ is a sovereign self-hosted file sync, share, and collaboration platform maintained by the Heinlein Group. It is a fork of the OpenCloud Infinite Scale codebase and is published as the ``opencloudeu/opencloud`` container image."
msgstr "`OpenCloud <https://opencloud.eu/>`__ er en suverene selvvært filsynkronisering, aksje- og samarbeidsplattform som vedlikeholdes av Heinlein Group. Det er en gaffel av OpenCloud Infinite Scale codebase og er publisert som ``opencloudeu/opencloud`` Beholderbilde."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`OpenTalk <https://opentalk.eu/>`__ is a sovereign open-source video conferencing platform developed by the Heinlein Group. It combines a Rust controller, a LiveKit-based WebRTC media server, and a React web frontend."
msgstr "`OpenTalk <https://opentalk.eu/>`__ er en suverene videokonferanseplattform utviklet av Heinlein Group. Det kombinerer en Rust kontroller, en LiveKit-basert WebRTC medieserver, og en React web frontend."

msgid "`OutboundEmailAccounts` names SuiteCRM's outbound mail module and declares the `email` bridge. The role configures no SMTP, so the addon records the bridge rather than a provisioned integration, and [`files/playwright/addons/OutboundEmailAccounts.spec.js`](./files/playwright/addons/OutboundEmailAccounts.spec.js) stays skipped until an install path writes the transport of the mail server `web-app-email` selects into the legacy mailer settings."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` : Social Home 2026.6.16 imports `logout` from `client/src/store/auth.ts` in exactly one place —   `client/src/main.tsx` wires it as the 401 handler via `setUnauthorizedHandler(logout)`. No   component renders a logout control, so `personas/utils/logout.js` has nothing to click and the   admin journey cannot complete. The alternative — injecting a `[data-injected-logout]` button via   `templates/javascript.js.j2` — was rejected: the model   (`roles/web-app-prometheus/templates/javascript.js.j2`) points the button at   `OIDC.CLIENT.LOGOUT_URL`, which only exists for OIDC-gated roles, and this role deliberately runs   without SSO. Path back: upstream ships a logout control (or an in-app logout endpoint we can   target), then drop the flag and keep the `adminInteraction` already wired in the spec."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` : sosialt hjem 2026.6.16 import `logout` fra `client/src/store/auth.ts` På akkurat ett sted — `client/src/main.tsx` ledninger som 401 Håndterer via `setUnauthorizedHandler(logout)`. Ingen komponent gjør en utloggingskontroll, så `personas/utils/logout.js` har ingenting å klikke på, og admin reisen kan ikke fullføres. Alternativ - injisering `[data-injected-logout]` via `templates/javascript.js.j2` — ble avvist: Modellen (`roles/web-app-prometheus/templates/javascript.js.j2`) punkter knappen på `OIDC.CLIENT.LOGOUT_URL`, som bare eksisterer for OIDC-baserte roller, og denne rollen kjører med vilje uten SSO. Sti tilbake: oppstrøms skip en utlogging kontroll (eller et utloggingsendepunkt i appen vi kan målrette), deretter slippe flagget og holde `adminInteraction` allerede koblet i spesifikasjonen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` is declared because the shared helper cannot reach Shopware's logout, not because the journey is untestable. The only logout control lives in `.sw-admin-menu__user-actions`, which the administration stylesheet keeps at `display: none` until its toggle is clicked, and that toggle is a bare `div` carrying no role, no `aria-haspopup` and no dropdown class — nothing in the helper's trigger set matches it. Its second fallback, following a same-origin settings link, misses as well because the administration is hash-routed and every settings target is `#/sw/settings/...`."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` erklært fordi den delte hjelperen ikke kan nå ShopwareUtloggingen, ikke fordi reisen ikke kan testes. Den eneste utloggingskontrollen lever i `.sw-admin-menu__user-actions`, som administrasjonsstilen holder på `display: none` til dens bryter er klikket, og den bryteren er en bar `div` å ha ingen rolle, nei `aria-haspopup` og ingen dropdown-klasse - ingenting i hjelperens utløser sett passer det. Dens andre tilbakefall, etter en samme origin innstillinger link, savner også fordi administrasjonen er hash-routed og alle innstillinger målet er `#/sw/settings/...`.."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` is declared for a second, independent reason, and two separate obstacles justify it."
msgstr "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true` er erklært av en annen, uavhengig grunn, og to separate hindringer rettferdiggjør det."

msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2` stays true although the header login now signs the administrator in after the Keycloak round trip; the shared admin flow has not been run against it. Options: run the shared admin flow against the SSO variant and unblock the administrator persona when it passes."
msgstr ""

msgid "`PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2` still cites a missing staff account; `tasks/01_site.yml` now provisions the administrator as superuser with the `admin` and `moderator` groups, so only the icon-only logout dropdown remains as the blocker. Options: give the shared in-app-logout helper a match for `details#navbar-dropdown` or label the control, then unblock both personas."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` : The app authenticates against its own `platform_users` table. There is no OIDC client and no   auto-provisioning, so the biber account never exists inside Social Home. Path back: upstream   grows an OIDC/trusted-header auth path."
msgstr "`PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` : Appen godkjenner mot sin egen `platform_users` Bord. Det er ingen OIDC-klient og ingen auto-provisioning, så Biber-kontoen eksisterer aldri inne Social Home. Vei tilbake: oppstrøms vokser en OIDC/trusted-header auth bane."

