# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: immutable kildekontrakt av en lagereide adapter. ``category_allowlist`` passer til en oppstrøms som bytter hele kategorier og tilbyr ikke noe per verktøyfilter, hvor en verktøy-tillatelsesliste ville være upåvirkelig; ``mcp_passthrough`` foran en oppstrøms som allerede snakker MCP i stedet for å oversette REST. ``upstream_path`` navn som oppstrøms der det bor på programmets egen vhost, slik at proxyen kan skjule det: å nå det direkte går forbi tillatelseslisten adapteren eksisterer for å håndheve. En leverandør hvis oppstrøms er en separat sidebil erklærer ``upstream_network`` I stedet og har ingenting å skjule der."

msgid "``administrator`` opens the datasource administration. ``files/playwright/test-logs.js`` writes a line into the reverse proxy’s access log and finds it in Explore (the probe value travels in the request path; the proxy logs no query string), and proves that an ``auditor`` member reads logs while every write to datasources, dashboards and alert rules is refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "``agent``: the agent holds the master key itself and works fully autonomously; this is an explicit release set per role in the inventory."
